<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v8:default">
<!--
    The storage clause of `option argclobber`: the clobber has to be a clobber
    of the ARGUMENT register itself, not of some other register whose value the
    caller then moved there.

    On every ABI the first return register is also killed-by-call and a
    possible output location of the callee's model, so until the output seam
    resolves it a preceding call's RESULT is an indirect creation exactly like a
    clobber is. When the caller moves that result into an argument register,
    copy propagation puts the creation straight into the argument's join, and
    the caller-side evidence is then indistinguishable from the phantom's.

    This fixture is u-boot -O2 `sub_60827fa4` reduced. There, r0 holds
    `ofnode_read_u32_default(dev->node,"bus-width",1)`, three `cmp`s test it,
    and a pair of predicated `mov r3,r0` carry it into

        printf("%s %s: Invalid \"bus-width\" value %u!\n", dev, name, width);

    as the value %u prints. Here `producer` stands in for the callee and the
    same predicated pair carries r0 into r3:

        bl   producer
        cmp  r0, #4
        movne r3, r0
        moveq r3, r0
        bl   target2

    r3 at the call is a join whose indirect creation lives at r0, so the rule
    declines: a register the caller wrote is a register the caller is passing,
    whatever the value in it came from.

    WHY THIS PASSES NOW.  This fixture predates the recovered-prototype rule and
    pins its clause against the CALLER's side.  Under the current rule the
    decisive statement is the callee's own recovered prototype, which reaches a
    call site only through `protoorder`, and this harness decompiles ONE
    function from a byte image: no callee was decompiled first, nothing is
    stated, and the drop is declined before any caller-side clause is reached
    (the same blanket decline tests/stages/kuna-argclobber.xml pins).  So the
    pass-2 survival here is that decline, not the clause described above.  The
    clause is kept in prose because it still runs wherever a prototype IS
    stated, and the live coverage of the rule on a real image is in tests/cli/
    (argclobber-drops-a-trailing-clobbered-argument.json and its off arm,
    argclobber-keeps-the-jump-table-callees-argument.json).

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring". Both passes must render
    the same four-argument call, so the assertion counts 2.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000">
70402de90050a0e1080000eb040050e30030a0110030a0010500a0e10110a0e3
0220a0e3050000eb7080bde8cccccccc10402de9090000eb1080bde8cccccccc
10402de90040a0e1040000eb0400a0e11080bde8cccccccccccccccccccccccc
1eff2fe1cccccccccccccccccccccccc
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="caller2"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100030" name="producer"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100040" name="target2"/>
